cation pass on the compiled\n  artifact, deterministic enforcement co-located with the tool-mediation\n  chokepoint, and purpose-based access control. In v1.3 it adds activation-layer\n  defense-in-depth: control-vector steering and refusal-direction\n  integrity attestation beneath the deterministic gate. The pattern is\n  defined as fourteen principles plus reference SLAs and a numbered\n  build sequence.\n  It is the fifth specification in the nine-spec SaaSquach AI Labs catalog\n  alongside PDS, ACS, ESF, CRI, DCS, GDS, ARS, and SRS.\nkeywords:\n  - agent-governance\n  - policy-as-code\n  - opa\n  - cedar\n  - spiffe\n  - did\n  - audit\n  - tamper-evident\n  - owasp-agentic\n  - deterministic-enforcement\n  - llm-architecture\n","encoding":"utf-8","sha":"af7df7f05a7908868983cf405cc6d84f01e2aaa3","display_url":"https://github.com/drewmattie-code/Agent-Governance-Spine/blob/815256cee74afe25edf32a344abe42ea63f9bf68/CITATION.cff","display_title":"CITATION.cff"}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
